{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggkcbFVioGcGVBWHCH4t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The ground state changes from high spin (⁴T₁g) to low spin (²E_g) at Dq ≈ 1958 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Method.** I diagonalised the full d⁷ problem numerically instead of using the Tanabe–Sugano matrices. I included the electron repulsion and an octahedral field in the basis of all 2-electron determinants with M_s = ½ (the 7-electron states), with these inputs:\n\n- B = 922 cm⁻¹ and C = 4156 cm⁻¹ fix the Slater–Condon integrals.\n- Octahedral field: ⟨±2|V|±2⟩ = Dq, ⟨±1|V|±1⟩ = −4Dq, ⟨0|V|0⟩ = 6Dq, and ⟨2|V|−2⟩ = 5Dq.\n\nI separated quartet and doublet states using ⟨S²⟩. The lowest quartet is ⁴T₁g and the lowest doublet is ²E_g. I then solved for the Dq where their energies are equal.\n\n**Result.** The quartet energy minus the doublet energy is:\n\n| Dq (cm⁻¹) | E(⁴T₁g) − E(²E_g) (cm⁻¹) |\n|---|---|\n| 1500 | −4478 |\n| 2000 | +412 |\n\nThe sign change gives the crossing at Dq ≈ 1958 cm⁻¹, which is Dq/B ≈ 2.12. This is consistent with the known crossover near Dq/B ≈ 2.1 for C/B = 4.5.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1958, \"B\": 922, \"C\": 4156, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Full d7 octahedral matrix diagonalisation gives the 4T1g to 2Eg ground-state crossing at Dq ≈ 1958 cm^-1.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1631,"cache_read_input_tokens":6423,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1631,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8f5dccc-056d-4050-962e-f02751aee4e0","uuid":"cb3387b6-a729-4bda-9860-03f50a065c69","timestamp":"2026-11-03T22:05:05.007Z","request_id":"req_011Cggkcax97f8k2UsCjyAAN"}
